  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "WBNchYFrajdxOX3asstbilRoA1g=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:13.473Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "SDC was a member-bank-owned Danish cooperative and has been sold to Netcompany. That removes it as an independent lead \u2014 the ownership structure that made it interesting no longer exists \u2014 and it places it inside a firm the research elsewhere reads as the closest competitor rather than a channel.\n\nThe wider reading the record draws is that the cooperative model is consolidating. Several Danish bank-owned cooperatives appear in this lead set as a distinct structural category, and one of them has now been acquired by a large bespoke-build integrator. If that direction continues, the window for engaging owner-controlled Nordic financial IT is narrowing rather than stable.\n\nIts stack was not researched. The entry is kept for the pattern rather than for the prospect, at priority 4.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- SDC (DK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> ACQUIRED. Was member-bank-owned; sold to Netcompany. The cooperative model is consolidating.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:13.473533Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:13.473537Z"
    }
  },
